<title>SWEDEN: Swedish NCC sells Duesseldorf offices.</title>
<headline>Swedish NCC sells Duesseldorf offices.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish construction firm NCC said on Thursday that it has sold a first phase of an office development in the German city of Duesseldorf for 450 million crowns to a German construction fund company.  </p>
<p>The company said in a statement that the offices were in a development in central Duesseldorf and accounted for 20,000 square metres of the 80,000 square metre development.</p>
<p>The development has offices, shops and a hotel.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +468 700 1003</p>
</text>
